Get the image on the nodes of the object not running the container, so a
failover finds it in the store of the engine, and neither waits for the
registry nor fails with it.

If not set, the `node.image_prefetch` keyword of the node decides, `true`
by default.

The image prefetched by a node is the `image` keyword as this node
evaluates it, the one its start would run. It is fetched when the store of
the engine does not hold it, and never fetched again once there.

The image is copied from another node of the object holding it, and pulled
from its registry when none does. The nodes asked are the ones of the
`nodes` keyword, the ones where the container is up first, of the
architecture of the node. A cluster with no registry is so served: load
the image on a node, start the object there, and the other nodes copy it.
The `registry_creds` are not used for a copy.

A node holding the image in the store of another engine is asked too,
docker and podman reading the archive of each other, when the image names
its registry. A podman image naming none, as `nginx`, is copied from the
podman of the other nodes only: docker reads that name as an image of the
Docker Hub, where podman resolves it with its `registries.conf`.

A copy is the image as the other node holds it: a moving tag as `latest`
is not refreshed from the registry, neither by a copy nor once the image
is there, and the nodes may hold different builds of it. Pin a tag that
does not move, or a digest, for the nodes to run the same build.

The prefetch is a best effort, done by the daemon when the configuration
of the object changes. A prefetch that failed is tried again later, less
and less often, and the resource status warns of the missing image
meanwhile. An image removed from the store, as by an `image prune`, is
fetched again, except from the store of a `rootless_user`, which the
daemon does not watch: that one is fetched again on the next change of
the configuration.

A start is not changed by the prefetch: it pulls a missing image, and
`image_pull_policy = always` still pulls at every start.
